From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:29:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(goldens): path query over every session, the core types,
 both file formats, a schema check on every transform

query@site-example and query@cache-sync run the site's own example
through path query (all seven harnesses; cache sync over five real
stores, incremental). core_types@dag and core_types@validate pin the
RFC's DAG features and what path p validate enforces: five RFC rules it
accepts are pinned as gaps with qualifier concerns. formats@<set> streams
every golden document to .path.jsonl and seals it back unchanged;
formats@examples pins the graph.id difference and fixes the drifted
path-02 example. validate_transforms@<set>/@writers validate every
transform's document against the base and v1.1.0 kind schemas; the
bundled kind schema is byte-identical to the published one.
